        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2f40bdcb-d12e-5a56-a370-261a85d33706",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Foale, Charles Simonyi, Eileen Collins, Bernard A. Harris Jr.\n- Organizations: NASA\n- Missions: STS-63, Soyuz TMA-14, Space Shuttle missions, Mir missions, International Space Station missions, STS-71\n- Places: Mir, International Space Station\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Foale was born on 6 January 1957 and is a British-American astrophysicist and former NASA astronaut.\n- Michael Foale is a veteran of six Space Shuttle missions and extended missions on both Mir and the International Space Station.\n- STS-63 was the 20th mission of Discovery and a night launch.\n- STS-63 was the first Space Shuttle mission with a female pilot, Eileen Collins.\n- STS-63 included the first EVAs by UK-born astronaut Michael Foale and by U.S. astronaut of African heritage Bernard A. Harris Jr.\n- STS-63 successfully deployed and retrieved the Spartan-204 platform and conducted a scheduled rendezvous and flyaround of Mir in preparation for STS-71, the first mission to dock with Mir.\n- In March 2009, Charles Simonyi made his second trip to the International Space Station aboard Soyuz TMA-14.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ee5790af-ed62-5718-9b7f-c74d6f194ae0",
        "text": "Page: Michael Foale. Sentence: Colin Michael Foale, CBE (born 6 January 1957) is a British-American astrophysicist and former NASA astronaut.\nPage: Michael Foale. Sentence: He is a veteran of six Space Shuttle missions and extended missions on both Mir and the International Space Station.\nPage: Charles Simonyi. Sentence: In March 2009, aboard Soyuz TMA-14, he made a second trip to the International Space Station.\nPage: STS-63. Sentence: A night launch and the 20th mission for \"Discovery\", it marked the first time a Space Shuttle mission had a female pilot, Eileen Collins, the first EVAs for both a UK born astronaut Michael Foale and a US astronaut of African heritage Bernard A. Harris, Jr. and it also carried out the successful deployment and retrieval of the Spartan-204 platform, along with the scheduled rendezvous and flyaround of \"Mir\", in preparation for STS-71, the first mission to dock with \"Mir\".",
